    <DataNode elementId="AT2G03220-MONOMER" textLabel="α-1,2-fucosyltransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SWH5" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, karthik">Xyloglucan &amp;alpha;-1,2-fucosyltransferase is a glycosyltransferase family 37 (GT37) enzyme that adds the terminal fucosyl residue on xyloglucan side chains in many plants. The enzyme was originally was purified from pea epicotyls, and the homologous |FRAME: AT2G03220| gene was identified in |FRAME: TAX-3702| |CITS: [10373113]|. The gene was cloned and expressed in COS cells, and xyloglucan &amp;alpha;-1,2-fucosyltransferase activity was demonstrated in the cell extracts |CITS: [11854459]|. Cell walls of |FRAME: TAX-3702| mutants lacking |FRAME: AT2G20370| contain less than 2% of the wild-type amount of fucosylated xyloglucan. Despite this alteration in structure, mur2 plants show a normal growth habit and wall strength |CITS: [11854459]|. Several related enzymes have been discovered, but do not appear to be involved in xyloglucan synthesis |CITS: [11743104]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G03220-MONOMER" />
